.TH SDL_HINT_MAC_OPENGL_ASYNC_DISPATCH 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_MAC_OPENGL_ASYNC_DISPATCH \- A variable controlling whether dispatching OpenGL context updates should block the dispatching thread until the main thread finishes processing on macOS.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_MAC_OPENGL_ASYNC_DISPATCH \(dqSDL_MAC_OPENGL_ASYNC_DISPATCH\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: Dispatching OpenGL context updates will block the dispatching thread until the main thread finishes processing\[char46] (default)
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: Dispatching OpenGL context updates will allow the dispatching thread to continue execution\[char46]
.PP
Generally you want the default, but if you have OpenGL code in a background thread on a Mac, and the main thread hangs because it\(aqs waiting for that background thread, but that background thread is also hanging because it\(aqs waiting for the main thread to do an update, this might fix your issue\[char46]
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

